Google Cloud Compute Engine doesn’t offer the **RTX A6000** as an attachable GPU, so an API request for that exact configuration won’t succeed. Here’s a Compute Engine REST API example for a supported alternative: an **NVIDIA L4** with **Ubuntu 20.04 LTS**. This uses a `g2-standard-4` machine type.

```bash
PROJECT_ID="your-project-id"
ZONE="us-central1-a"
INSTANCE="ubuntu-l4"

curl -X POST \
  "https://compute.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/zones/${ZONE}/instances" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d "{
    \"name\": \"${INSTANCE}\",
    \"machineType\": \"zones/${ZONE}/machineTypes/g2-standard-4\",
    \"disks\": [{
      \"boot\": true,
      \"autoDelete\": true,
      \"initializeParams\": {
        \"sourceImage\": \"projects/ubuntu-os-cloud/global/images/family/ubuntu-2004-lts\"
      }
    }],
    \"networkInterfaces\": [{
      \"network\": \"global/networks/default\",
      \"accessConfigs\": [{\"type\": \"ONE_TO_ONE_NAT\", \"name\": \"External NAT\"}]
    }]
  }"
```

Replace the project and zone values, and check that the selected zone offers G2 instances. The `g2-standard-4` includes an L4 GPU; it is **not** an RTX A6000.
